From 6d71c2fb74f0762d5d4ff1f75ce0ba9cb2558e4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:09:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rkcif: allow cache hints

Without an ISP, the raw frames captured by the VICAP are processed by
the CPU, and reading them through the uncached mapping of the default
MMAP buffers is slow. Set allow_cache_hints so that userspace can
request non-coherent buffers with V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT;
videobuf2 performs the cache maintenance when buffers are queued and
dequeued. On the RV1126 this raises a software debayer pipeline
streaming 1080p JPEG from 13.3 to 19.1 frames per second.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkcif/rkcif-stream.c
@@ -513,6 +513,7 @@ static int rkcif_stream_init_vb2_queue(s
 {
 	q->type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE;
 	q->io_modes = VB2_MMAP | VB2_DMABUF;
+	q->allow_cache_hints = 1;
 	q->drv_priv = stream;
 	q->ops = &rkcif_stream_vb2_ops;
 	q->mem_ops = &vb2_dma_contig_memops;
